IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg1-seat`

-- The one expectation in this piece that is meant to fail; check.sh lists it in expected_failed with the count 1.
-- It records the author's first reading of section 110(i) from the text: that when a quorum cannot be readily convened
-- only a majority of the directors present may act, so that the board's own action does not count.
-- The text does not decide between that reading and the one the rule takes (NOTES, Fork register, F32), so
-- dg1-cases-seat.l4 asserts the reading taken, and this assertion is kept here, failing, so that both readings are on record.
-- Inputs, in the order of the question: the emergency; a quorum can readily be convened; the board acted; a majority of the directors present acted.

§ `The first reading of section 110(i), kept as a failing expectation`

#ASSERT NOT (`May the board act on the stockholders' meeting during an emergency condition` `a nuclear or atomic disaster` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
